menu "Companion input (knob)"

    config COMPANION_ENABLE
        bool "Enable companion knob UDP input"
        default n
        help
            Starts the UDP listener + mDNS advertisement (_moonclock._udp
            .local) that accepts the companion knob's binary frames. The
            listener only queues; the UI tick drains it.

    config COMPANION_TOKEN
        int "Shared token byte (0 = accept any frame)"
        range 0 255
        default 0
        depends on COMPANION_ENABLE
        help
            LAN-trusted posture: this byte keeps a curious neighbour off
            the dial, it is not a secret. Both sides must set it (knob
            side: knob/sdkconfig.defaults). 0 accepts any token.

    config COMPANION_PORT
        int "UDP listen port"
        range 1024 65535
        default 50188
        depends on COMPANION_ENABLE

    config COMPANION_KEEP_WIFI
        bool "Keep WiFi associated while companion is active (wall-powered boards)"
        default n
        depends on COMPANION_ENABLE
        help
            The clock normally runs airplane-first: the radio comes up
            only for the boot/on-demand sync and the airplane / light
            sleep hand-offs deinitialize it. That makes the UDP listener
            unreachable between syncs. With this option those hand-offs
            leave the radio ASSOCIATED, so the knob can deliver frames
            at any time. Costs radio power: right for the wall-powered
            P4 4C, wrong for the battery S3 (leave n). Deep sleep always
            deinits (the companion is useless while the clock is hidden).

endmenu
